/*
 * Description  : A sub-millisecond row survives a predicate written at the value it displays
 * Expected Res : Success
 */

// Every row's ts carries a sub-millisecond remainder the reader truncates away, so row 1234 reads back as
// 1970-01-01T00:00:01.234Z while the file stores 1234456 microseconds. Pushing the instant that literal names
// excludes the row group holding it and this returns nothing; pushing the whole millisecond it denotes keeps it.
// Asserted on the rows returned rather than on a count, because a lost row is the failure mode.

USE test;

SELECT VALUE r.id FROM RowGroups r WHERE r.ts = datetime("1970-01-01T00:00:01.234Z");
